This folder contains the scripts used in the processing of the data of the manuscript. Here is a list of such scripts and a brief description:

cestrem.sh
# The objective of the script is to find the homologs groups that contain sequences from the species of interest

Detected.sh
 The objective of this script is to count Homologs Groups (HGs) that contain:
#      - Proteins detected by proteomics in one species
#      - Proteins detected in one species with an homolog in the other species
#      - Proteins detected in one species with an homolog detected in the other species as well

Processor.pl
# This Perl script renames sequence headers in a FASTA file. The script takes a FASTA file and adds a prefix followed by an incremental number to each sequence header.

SeqCounter.sh
# The objective is to count sequences from species of interest in Homologs Groups

SpeciesSearch.sh
# The goal of this script is to search for proteins identified by proteomics in homologous groups and list those groups that contain tegumentary proteins

TALsDomains.sh
# The objective of the script is to extract the protein domains present in Tegument Antigen Like (TAL) proteins

DDscript.sh
# The goal of this AI generated script is to search for proteins identified by proteomics within homologs groups (HGs) and list those groups

FisherTest.r
# Pfam Domain Enrichment Analysis (Fisher's Test)

SharedGenes.sh
# The goal of this script is to make a list of shared genes between the tegument of H. microstoma, M. corti and E.multilocularis, grouped by homologous groups

SppCounter.sh
# The goal of this script is to find, among the homologs groups (output files from get_homologues), those that have sequences from the species I want